[7.300791,"o","Verified against the primary records. Here is the answer.\r\n\r\n## Why ohya replaced the embedded Headscale stack\r\n\r\nA live two-machine test on 2026-11-16 (session `da4c3317`, device `05b0ff2c`, this VM) showed that \"real Tailcat\" (a `tailscale.com`-based address transport) met the project's join-ability goal, and the tsnet+Headscale design did not:\r\n\r\n1. **Joining was too hard under Headscale.** The tsnet plus Headscale design is why a hub needs a reachable control URL and a trusted TLS certificate (event **2665994**, NOTES entry). The spike proved a Mac could reach the VM hub with only a 233-character address \u2014 no account, no Tailscale install, no open ports, no certificates \u2014 and all 32 MiB of test data arrived (event **2665998**).\r\n2. **The cost was acceptable.** Indirect paths (phone hotspot behind double NAT) fell back to Tailscale's public relay at 3.1\u20133.3 Mbit/s versus 8\u201312 Mbit/s direct. Daily sync is fine on the relay; only the first history upload is slow (event **2665998**).\r\n3. **The recorded decision.** \"Replace the Headscale stack with real Tailcat\" \u2014 the test proved the main point, and Tailcat matches what `MANIFESTO.md` already promises as \"Embedded Tailcat\", so the change brings the code in line with the project's intent (event **2667494**). The plan: a new ADR superseding ADRs 0002 (tailcat transport) and 0006 (shared device transport), keeping the device registry as the only authorization boundary, and swapping `internal/transport` adapters to `tailcat.Server`/`tailcat.Client`.\r\n\r\nFollow-through: `docs/adr/0011-tailcat-address-transport.md` and `0012-two-step-multi-machine-setup.md` now exist in the ADR index (event **2716304**), and the old embedded control package (`internal/control`, Headscale + embedded DERP in `serve`, per event 156241) is the stack being replaced.\r\n\r\nCitations: events 2667494, 2665998, 2665994 (session `claude-code:05b0ff2c233cb6a22d24cb1722f9204f:da4c3317-\u2026`, 2026-11-16), 2716304 (ADR index), 156241 (old embedded control package), 155439 (ADR 0002 context).\r\n"]
